 "knowledge-03": [
  {
   "step": 0,
   "user": "does meditation actually help with anxiety or is it just hype?",
   "status": 201,
   "reply": "Meditation isn’t just hype—it does have a real effect on anxiety.  Research summarized by the NCCIH notes that mindfulness‑based practices can reduce anxiety symptoms and tend to work better than doing nothing at all, sometimes matching the benefits of established therapies like cognitive‑behavioral therapy [S1].  A review of multiple studies on relaxation‑type techniques (which include many meditation approaches) also found that they lower anxiety, depression, and worry, and in some cases even outperform CBT for certain anxiety disorders, though the evidence isn’t uniform across every condition [S3].  So while it’s not a magic cure, meditation does show genuine, measurable benefits for many people dealing with anxiety.",
   "safety_pathway": null,
